        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "Bipolarity defines the Toronto Blue Jays' latest Seattle trip, a tale of two games that left them back in the shadow of the.500 mark. After Dylan Cease spun seven scoreless innings to blank the Mariners 2-0, the offense imploded the very next day, surrendering an 11-0 disaster marked by Randy Arozarena's grand slam and three Mariners home runs. The Jays now sit at 42-47, 11.5 games behind in the AL East, with their one-game win streak overshadowed by a five-game under-.500 reality. Vladimir Guerrero Jr. remains the story, though he recently declined an All-Star invite while Cease and Varland head to the game. <strong>The 11-0 blowout to the Mariners</strong> stands as the latest wound in a season that demands urgency. <strong>Tonight's rematch at 5:00 PM ET against Seattle</strong> offers a chance to reset the series before the All-Star break looms.",
        "updated": "Updated July 5, 2026"
