      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The Toronto Raptors are no longer just surviving; they're rebuilding with purpose, and the first real brick in that new foundation has just been laid. <strong>Jaden Bradley, the 50th pick in last week's draft, has agreed to a two-way deal</strong>, instantly injecting young energy into a roster that finished 46-36 and third in the Atlantic Division. Bradley, a 22-year-old guard from Arizona who earned Big 12 Player of the Year honors, posted career highs of 13.3 points and 39.4% from three - numbers that suggest he could be a late-round steal. With Scotty Pippen Jr. and Garrett Temple moving on to coaching roles, the front office is clearly prioritizing youth and two-way flexibility. <strong>What to watch now is how quickly Bradley adapts to the Raptors 905 system and whether he earns a Summer League spotlight</strong> - a critical step for a player the team sees as a long-term asset.",
